  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 158 AM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nTemperatures steadily decrease through weekend with highs in the\n70s and 80s for Saturday and Sunday. This will be a welcome\nbreak from the heat especially with low temperatures in the 60s.\nNorthwesterly winds will be breezy ahead of and after the\nfrontal passage. Saturday will be breezy with winds gusting near\n30 mph through the day. Sunday will still feature breezy winds\nnear 20 mph out of the northeast. High pressure begins to build\nin again on Sunday, but temperatures take their time warming as\nwe go into next week. Highs will be in the upper 80s to lower \n90s to start the week with mid to upper 90s returning by mid-\nweek. Mostly dry weather is expected as we start August.",
